# Conditional fixed Wave151 full99 equality encoding

This encoding concerns exactly the immutable Wave151 Q1 incidence factor,
with the triangle-root partial graph and562 forced assignments authenticated
by a separate independent assembly/propagation audit. No arbitrary target is
asserted to contain this factor, and no automorphism of a target is assumed.

The model's symmetric99x99 ternary matrix prescribes fixed zeros/ones and
exactly1,928 free unordered entries. Each free entry has one distinct Boolean
edge variable; all fixed entries, diagonal zeros and variable mappings are
compared in full against the independent scope input.

For every unordered pair u,v, expand A_uv plus the scalar product of rows u,v.
Fixed zeros delete terms, fixed ones contribute an integer constant or a single
edge variable, and each remaining product is represented by a bidirectional
AND. The checker reconstructs every term directly from the raw matrix and
derives each gate's CNF from its complete Boolean truth relation. It does not
import the producer's clause templates. The previously independently authored
truth-relation checker is reused, with its exact source hash disclosed.

Every counter state at(i,j) asserts that the first i inputs contain at least j
true values. Its recurrence is S(i,j)=S(i-1,j) OR (x_i AND S(i-1,j-1)). Boundary
values are exact constants. Bidirectional gate equivalence proves these meanings
inductively and gives a unique auxiliary extension. For bound b, imposing the
final b-th threshold and forbidding the final(b+1)-th threshold imposes exact
equality; b=0 uses the true constant for the lower threshold. The complete
checker verifies all states, fresh variable allocation and literal raw clauses.

The99 degree rows impose degree14. The4,851 unordered pair rows impose
A_uv+(A^2)_uv=2, each exactly. Thus every model decodes to a binary symmetric
zero-diagonal graph with off-diagonal identity A^2=12I-A+2J; the diagonal is14
because a binary row's squared norm is its degree. Conversely any target
extending the specified partial graph satisfies all rows and uniquely supplies
the AND and threshold variables. The independent propagation premise connects
the final ternary matrix to the original fixed Q1 completion question.

This is an equivalence for one conditional instance, not its satisfiability or
an unrestricted theorem of nonexistence. A future SAT result requires a separate
complete assignment/raw graph checker. UNSAT requires the complete saved proof,
checker identity and independent replay against this exact CNF. Historical
unproved UNSAT labels are not premises.

This checking path adapts the frozen independently authored Wave154 checker
and reuses its independently authored GateAudit truth-relation helper. It
does not constitute another independent implementation of that shared helper.
The complete changed scope and all changed raw clauses are checked afresh.
The exact Wave151 initial/final matrices,562 propagation steps and archive
factor key are bound to the separate two-case propagation audit; no archive
UNSAT claim or historical verification label is used as a premise.

